DSEAMS

fix dseams reads the running LAMMPS atoms and calls libyodaLib through
seams_insitu.h. The header and the source are GPL-2.0-only because they
include LAMMPS headers. libyodaLib is not part of this package.

Enable the package with PKG_DSEAMS and pass the library location:

  -D PKG_DSEAMS=on
  -D SEAMS_INCLUDE=<directory that contains seams_insitu.h>
  -D SEAMS_LIBRARY=<path to libyodaLib.so>

The fix keyword host defaults to yes and uses the LAMMPS neighbour list.
host no leaves that list unused so the engine builds its own.

fix ID group dseams record PATH neigh PATH every N cutoff X depth N host yes|no

record is required. neigh is optional. Without neigh, no neighbour file
is written. With neigh, each analysed step appends one block:

  frame
  step STEP
  cutoff X
  box xlo ylo zlo lx ly lz xy xz yz
  pbc bx by bz
  host 0|1
  atoms N
  atom id type x y z
  row id neighbour ...
  endframe

host 0 means that step built no list. A row starts with the central id.
The other ids are the neighbours kept for the fix group. pbc uses the
LAMMPS boundary code. Zero is periodic.

The separate CHILL+ compute, when built as a plugin, accepts

  compute ID group dseams file PATH cutoff X graph cutoff|mutual

Without file, it writes no label file. With file, each evaluation
appends one block of `label id type x y z code`. The code is 0 cubic,
1 hexagonal, 2 water, 3 interfacial, 4 clathrate, 5 interClathrate,
6 unclassified, 7 reCubic, 8 reHex.
